<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mosquito Coast</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mosquitia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mosquito Coast is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> lowland of eastern Nicaragua and north-eastern Honduras, home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miskito">Miskito people</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">Creole</a> and Garífuna communities. From the seventeenth century the Miskito kings were allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, which maintained a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over the coast. Britain recognised Honduran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the northern part in 1859 and Nicaraguan sovereignty over the rest in 1860, and Nicaragua incorporated the autonomous Mosquito Reserve by force in 1894.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mosquito-coast.jpg" alt="Mosquito Coast" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mapa Miskito.png: DaDez~commonswiki (talk · contribs) NIcaraguaGeneralV2.svg: Rowanwindwhistler (talk · contribs) der... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_Miskito-es.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
